WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:05.472
When you're

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:09.075
in Memphis, you got to do the ducks

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.211
If they sell, you definitely

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.480
have to come up and see the ceremony.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.049
It is an experience unlike any other.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.551
It's like the Ducks owned the hotel

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.656
The Duck March ceremony is exclusive

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:24.724
to the Peabody Hotel

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.526
in Memphis, Tennessee.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.363
There was General Manager back in 1933

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.965
that went on a duck hunting trip

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.700
with a friend of his over in Arkansas.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.734
As a practical joke,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.469
they decided to bring back the live

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.538
duck decoys that they were using

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.672
and set them loose inside.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.674
That found some of the general manager

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.842
woke back up the next morning

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.843
in the clear mind set.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.413
I'm sure he probably got up with his life

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.180
when he got down here.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.481
There was a crowd of people

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.616
standing around the fountain

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.117
staring at these dogs

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:53.253
that led to ducks living in the fountain.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.355
But then seven years later, a man

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.457
by the name of Edward Pembroke

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.091
just so happened

00:00:58.091 --> 00:00:59.259
that he was an animal trainer

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.860
in the Ringling Brothers and Barnum

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.629
and Bailey Circus as a young man.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:03.863
And he was the one that came up

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:04.564
with the idea

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.132
of turning the ducks,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.501
living in the fountain into a ceremony

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:11.704
I have

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.173
the honor and the pleasure

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.641
of marching the ducks for you

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:15.775
all this morning.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.410
My title here at the Peabody

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.612
Hotel is of the Duck Master,

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.814
a very unusual title.

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.415
The whole is my job to train

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.184
the team of ducks that we have here.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.885
And they have a $200,000

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:28.054
duck palace upstairs on the rooftop.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.323
Hey, good morning, Doug. Good morning.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.392
I hope everybody gets a good sleep.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.893
It's nighttime out.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.462
Is it going to be a great one?

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:37.230
A lot of people.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.533
It came a long way to see you all

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.235
This is a public ceremony,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.070
and it happens twice a day. Every day.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.339
One at 11:00 and one at 5 p.m.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.141
there would be in least

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:51.277
two to 300 people on the busy days.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.412
The number of people doing the duck

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.947
march. We're talking into the thousands

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:58.852
Ladies and

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.986
gentlemen, if I

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.087
may direct your attention

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.422
to the elevators,

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.157
having just left their penthouse

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.426
on the roof to join you.

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.627
Looking good.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.162
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.530
the march of the world

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.867
famous Peabody Ducks

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.602
all the way to the fountain.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.370
I need everybody to use the steps.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.339
Come on, Douglas. Let's do it.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.440
Everybody say good morning.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.042
Duffy's and

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.144
bad

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.079
and everybody use those steps for me.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.480
Everybody up the steps.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.281
Looking good.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:33.153
There's one, two, three, four and five.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:34.454
Great.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.522
Doggie

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.892
I have never seen anything like

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.560
the Peabody ducks around me

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.895
ever before in my life.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.129
We certainly do not have this

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:45.999
in Australia yet.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:46.399
With something

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.301
I'm probably never going to forget.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.469
Ever.

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.837
I'm now a duck.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.272
I'm a duck fan.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.674
To know you're providing

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:55.575
an experience

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.710
that's unlike any other is a privilege.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.012
Yeah, I don't consider it a job.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:02:59.913
I feel like it's

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.548
no pun intended, but it's a calling

